# Static image assets

Apply when adding or processing images under `static/` (especially `static/email/`).

## Transparency and backgrounds

- **Email illustrations** must use a **transparent PNG** — never ship a solid black or white matte behind artwork.
- Before committing uploaded artwork (e.g. Storyset/Freepik exports):
  1. Verify the file is true PNG with alpha (not JPEG renamed to `.png`).
  2. Remove near-black/near-white matte backgrounds so the shared email card background shows through.
  3. Crop to content bounds after transparency cleanup.
- Prefer saving email illustrations to `static/email/<descriptive-name>.png` and reference via `${origin}/email/<descriptive-name>.png`.

## Processing checklist

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| Format | Convert to PNG with alpha channel |
| Background | Remove solid black/white mats (threshold near-black pixels to transparent) |
| Crop | Trim empty transparent margins |
| Size | Reasonable dimensions for email (~600–800px wide max) |
| Naming | kebab-case, semantic (`team-invitation.png`, not `Invite-pana.png`) |

## Email usage

- Pair every new illustration with a sender in `src/lib/server/mail/` using `buildSimpleEmailHtml` / `illustrationUrl`.
- Follow `email-templates.mdc` for layout — do not embed images as base64 in HTML.

## UI usage

- Use `@lucide/svelte` icons for chrome; raster illustrations only for marketing/onboarding/email bands.
- Do not commit duplicate assets — reuse `static/email/` illustrations in UI when appropriate.

## Red flags (reject in review)

- JPEG saved as `.png` without alpha
- Solid black rectangle behind illustration in email
- Base64 image blobs in `.svelte` or mail templates
- One-off filenames that do not describe purpose
